# Request

User: when patching again, recheck whether the DeepSeek V4.1 Flash 1017 model is
added for use.

# Verified source

`https://ollama.com/library/deepseek-v4.1-flash/tags` lists two tags: `cloud`
(published 1 month ago) and **`1017-cloud`** (published 2 days ago, 1M context,
text+image input). The repository previously declared only the untagged
`deepseek-v4.1-flash` and the older `deepseek-v4-flash:0731` snapshot.

# Change

- `providers/ollama.py`: the Ollama Cloud offline default list now also contains
  `deepseek-v4.1-flash:1017-cloud`.
- `config_migrations.py`: marker `ollama_cloud_deepseek_v41_flash_1017_20261019`
  appends that model once to a saved `ollama-cloud.custom_models` list. It never
  changes `current_model`, and normalization deduplicates the `-cloud` suffix.
- `tests/test_ollama_cloud_new_models.py`, `tests/test_ollama_provider_options.py`:
  offline availability, one-time idempotent migration, and wire normalization
  (`deepseek-v4.1-flash:1017-cloud` → `deepseek-v4.1-flash:1017`).

# Verification

Focused isolated tests: 65 passed (`test_ollama_cloud_new_models`,
`test_ollama_provider_options`, `test_ollama_catalog`). No paid inference and no
live selection change. Model discovery from the official tags API remains the
authoritative source; the change only keeps the offline fallback complete.
